{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgufbod1fe","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"CDX-3 attempt claimed with force past the autowire judging gate; no eager judge without an active loop","summary":"CONTEXT for the judge of attempt orch/attempt/fbeb4c89-3ac8-44de-94c5-49a9793e27d5-5. The worker could not start_task normally: the node sat judging:true on a single provisional autowire context edge (note:note-mqbk7fr1oih, weight 0.5). routes/overlay.js:156 refuses an in_progress claim while (judging && !timedOut). The 10-min JUDGING_TIMEOUT_MS fallback never cleared because (a) next_action showed NO active loop, so the eager edge-judge never dispatches, and (b) each record_decision the worker made re-armed overlay.judgingSince via a fresh autowire edge, resetting the clock. On-disk overlay/checkpoint showed zero edges for the node — the provisional edges live only in the daemon's in-memory overlay, a memory/disk desync. Resolution: start_task force:true (the node was unclaimed, assignee:null, so force harmed no other agent; the !b.force arm at overlay.js:154 bypasses only the judging WAIT, not correctness). The single inherited note (harness capability matrix) was already read as context; the edge is a legitimate keep. Lesson: a worker dispatched against a judging-phase node with no active heartbeat loop must either force-claim or wait out a 10-min timeout it must not keep re-arming with note writes.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T16:15:13.117Z","vec":[-0.08891052007675171,0.04172007367014885,-0.04617777466773987,0.03265245258808136,0.08259344846010208,-0.022762451320886612,-0.007211950607597828,0.01885862834751606,0.007009825203567743,0.05787886306643486,0.00399600388482213,0.012872773222625256,-0.0033058766275644302,-0.003741712309420109,-0.03441894054412842,0.0033763153478503227,0.08618656545877457,-0.09224867075681686,-0.02875877544283867,0.008976588025689125,0.0440407320857048,-0.04378088563680649,0.0497891791164875,-0.020738273859024048,-0.043761115521